This crate embeds tables compiled from the third-party sources below
(the generated files under src/, made from the snapshots in the data/
directory of https://github.com/public/ducat). Each section names the
source, its version and the date it was retrieved.

[Unicode CLDR 49: spell-out rules (RBNF)]
  The rule-based number format spell-out rules of en, de, fr, es, it,
  nl and pt, from the Unicode Common Locale Data Repository (CLDR),
  release 49, as the cldr-rbnf 49.0.0 package publishes them,
  https://unpkg.com/cldr-rbnf@49.0.0/rbnf/<language>-SpelloutRules.txt
  The snapshot records no retrieval date; it was taken on 2026-11-08,
  the day it was added to the repository.
  Used under the Unicode License v3 (SPDX: Unicode-3.0), whose text is
  in LICENSE-UNICODE. Copyright © Unicode, Inc.

[Unicode CLDR 48: plurals, numbers and list patterns]
  Data from the Unicode Common Locale Data Repository (CLDR), release
  48, for the same seven languages: the cardinal and ordinal plural
  rules (supplemental/plurals.json, supplemental/ordinals.json), the
  group separator and minimum grouping digits (main/<language>/
  numbers.json), the standard two-item list pattern (main/<language>/
  listPatterns.json) and, with the cldr-names feature, each currency's
  display names by plural form (main/<language>/currencies.json, in
  src/names.rs), from the cldr-json 48.0.0 archive,
  https://github.com/unicode-org/cldr-json/releases/download/48.0.0/cldr-48.0.0-json-full.zip
  (sha256 25ab2651a1a874dd62a727d3c213d7c6bf0fc269b09d2937f0499b82d99fa58e),
  retrieved 2026-11-14.
  Used under the Unicode License v3 (SPDX: Unicode-3.0), whose text is
  in LICENSE-UNICODE. Copyright © Unicode, Inc.

